    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0277" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg203"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 26, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Pennington’s despatch of the 7th of
                    December, No. 2, has been received, and I have read with mingled emotions of
                    sorrow and pride the description it gives of the tributes so worthily paid in
                    Paris by the government of the Emperor and the foreign legations, and the press
                    of the metropolis, to the memory of William L. Dayton, esq., our late minister
                    to France.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM,H. SEWARD,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
